IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ofek-domain`

§ `The supplements`

-- ===========================================================================
-- What a teacher is paid ON TOP of the combined salary.
--
-- Three instruments, layered:
--
--   § 39 of the base agreement (25.12.2008) states the role supplements as
--   PERCENTAGES of the combined salary, and caps how many may be held at once.
--
--   § 10 of the wage agreement (19.10.2022) puts a SHEKEL FLOOR under five of
--   them from 1.9.2023: the supplement becomes "the higher of" the percentage
--   and a stated amount. This matters most at the bottom of the table, where
--   10% of a rank-1 salary is well under the floor.
--
--   §§ 5 and 22 of the same 2022 agreement add two NEW payments that are not
--   percentages of anything: Tosefet Ofek 2022, a shekel amount by rank, and
--   the school-role supplement, a shekel amount by units.
--
-- The distinction that runs through all of it is whether a payment IS part of
-- the combined salary. Tosefet Ofek 2022 is (2022 § 5.4), so it enters the
-- base of every percentage supplement and of the hourly value. The
-- school-role supplement is NOT (2022 § 22.11), so it enters neither.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Section 39 — the role supplements`

-- § 39(a)(1)-(11), as percentages of the combined salary. Two of them depend
-- on the stage of education and one on the size of the grade, which is why
-- this takes the teacher's own facts rather than the role alone.
GIVEN `the role` IS A `a role carrying a supplement`
      `the stage` IS A `a stage of education`
      `the classes in the grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 39 rate for` `the role` `the stage` `the classes in the grade`
    @nlg the section 39 rate for %the role%
    MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` THEN 10%    -- § 39(a)(1)
    WHEN `homeroom teacher of a first-grade class`                THEN 11.5%  -- § 39(a)(2)
    -- § 39(a)(5): 6% in a primary school, 8% in a junior high.
    WHEN `subject coordinator` THEN
        CONSIDER `the stage`
        WHEN `a primary school`     THEN 6%
        WHEN `a junior high school` THEN 8%
    WHEN `road-safety coordinator`  THEN 6%   -- § 39(a)(6)
    WHEN `security coordinator`     THEN 6%   -- § 39(a)(7)
    -- § 39(a)(8): 6% in a primary school, 10% in a junior high.
    WHEN `social-education coordinator` THEN
        CONSIDER `the stage`
        WHEN `a primary school`     THEN 6%
        WHEN `a junior high school` THEN 10%
    -- § 39(a)(9): 7% for a grade of up to 4 classes, 6% for more. The rate
    -- falls as the grade grows, which is the opposite direction to § 15's
    -- hours table, where a bigger grade buys MORE relief. Both are as
    -- printed.
    WHEN `grade-level coordinator` THEN
        IF `the classes in the grade` AT MOST 4 THEN 7% ELSE 6%
    WHEN `laboratory coordinator`                 THEN 3%   -- § 39(a)(10)
    WHEN `assessment and measurement coordinator` THEN 6%   -- § 39(a)(11)

-- § 39(b): "for the purposes of this section, other than sub-sections (a)(3)
-- and (a)(4), 'combined salary' means the combined salary for a FULL post
-- (100%), provided that the teacher was employed for at least 1/3 of a post."
--
-- This is the striking one, and it is not a rounding detail. A teacher on
-- half a post who is a homeroom teacher takes the FULL 10% of a full-post
-- salary, not half of it — the supplement attaches to the job, not to the
-- fraction. Below a third of a post it is not payable at all.
`the smallest post that carries a role supplement` MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY 3

GIVEN `the fraction of a full post` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the post carries the role supplements` IF
    `the fraction of a full post` AT LEAST `the smallest post that carries a role supplement`

-- § 39(c): at most TWO role supplements, unless the district director
-- approves a further one. The special education supplement is expressly not
-- counted for this purpose.
`the role supplements a teacher may hold` MEANS 2

GIVEN `the roles held` IS A NUMBER
      `the district director has approved a further supplement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of role supplements is allowed` IF
    IF `the district director has approved a further supplement`
        THEN `the roles held` AT MOST (`the role supplements a teacher may hold` PLUS 1)
        ELSE `the roles held` AT MOST `the role supplements a teacher may hold`

§§ `Section 10 of the 2022 agreement — the shekel floors`

-- From 1.9.2023 the homeroom and grade-coordinator supplements became "the
-- higher of" the § 39 percentage and a shekel amount. The floors are per
-- 2022 §§ 10.1.1.2 and 10.2.1.2.
`the date the shekel floors take effect` MEANS YMD 2023 9 1
`the floor under the homeroom supplement` MEANS 1_000          -- 2022 § 10.1.1.2
`the floor under the grade coordinator supplement` MEANS 1_100 -- 2022 § 10.2.1.2

GIVEN `the role` IS A `a role carrying a supplement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shekel floor under` `the role`
    @nlg the shekel floor under %the role%
    MEANS
    -- 2022 § 10 reaches five supplements. Three of them — young-division
    -- management, deputy headship and kindergarten management — are roles
    -- this encoding does not carry (NOTES.md § 4), so only the two that bear
    -- on a classroom teacher appear here. Every other § 39 supplement has no
    -- floor at all.
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` THEN `the floor under the homeroom supplement`
    WHEN `homeroom teacher of a first-grade class`                THEN `the floor under the homeroom supplement`
    WHEN `grade-level coordinator`                                THEN `the floor under the grade coordinator supplement`
    OTHERWISE                                                          0

GIVEN `the role` IS A `a role carrying a supplement`
      `the stage` IS A `a stage of education`
      `the classes in the grade` IS A NUMBER
      `the combined salary for a full post` IS A NUMBER
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the role supplement for` `the role` `the stage` `the classes in the grade` `the combined salary for a full post` `the date`
    @nlg the supplement payable for %the role%
    MEANS
    IF `the date` `is before` `the date the shekel floors take effect`
        THEN `the percentage amount`
        ELSE max `the percentage amount` (`the shekel floor under` `the role`)
    WHERE
        `the percentage amount` MEANS
            `the combined salary for a full post`
                TIMES (`the section 39 rate for` `the role` `the stage` `the classes in the grade`)

§§ `Section 5 of the 2022 agreement — Tosefet Ofek 2022`

-- A flat shekel amount by RANK, and it runs the opposite way to everything
-- else in this encoding: rank 1 gets the most and rank 9 gets nothing. It is
-- a levelling payment, compressing the bottom of the table toward the top,
-- and it doubled after its first year.
--
-- SOURCE, and again the corrected printing. The amounts below are appendices
-- bet-1/bet-2 (from 1.9.2022) and gimel-1/gimel-2 (from 1.9.2023) as reissued
-- to the AGORA by the follow-up committee decision of 14 January 2025. The
-- shekel printing at /tables/2022-09-01_ofek-hadash_tosefet-ofek-2022_BA.html
-- rounds these (793 for 792.77, 18 for 17.77).
--
-- THE SAME DECISION FIXES THE DATE. The 2022 agreement's appendix gimel
-- carried "1.1.23" as the date the increased amounts took effect; the
-- decision records this as a scribal error (ta'ut sofer) and corrects it to
-- 1.9.2023, which is the date used below.
--
-- The BA amounts fall by exactly 125 a rank and the 1.9.2023 figures are
-- exactly double the 1.9.2022 ones. The MA amounts fall by 131.25 a rank, and
-- their doubling is out by an agora at five of the nine ranks — the corpus's
-- provenance note attributes that to half-agora values in the underlying
-- figures rather than to a transcription error, and both printings are
-- reproduced here as they stand.
`the date tosefet ofek 2022 takes effect` MEANS YMD 2022 9 1
`the date tosefet ofek 2022 is increased` MEANS YMD 2023 9 1

GIVEN `the table` IS A `a salary table`
      `the rank` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2022 in` `the table` `the rank`
    @nlg Tosefet Ofek 2022 as it stood from September 2022 for rank %the rank%
    MEANS
    CONSIDER `the table`
    WHEN `the BA table — rating code 101` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the rank` AT MOST 1 THEN 792.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 2  THEN 667.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 3  THEN 542.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 4  THEN 417.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 5  THEN 292.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 6  THEN 167.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 7  THEN 92.77
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 8  THEN 17.77
               OTHERWISE                    0
    WHEN `the MA table — rating code 102` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the rank` AT MOST 1 THEN 832.44
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 2  THEN 701.19
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 3  THEN 569.94
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 4  THEN 438.69
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 5  THEN 307.44
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 6  THEN 176.19
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 7  THEN 97.44
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 8  THEN 18.69
               OTHERWISE                    0

GIVEN `the table` IS A `a salary table`
      `the rank` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2023 in` `the table` `the rank`
    @nlg Tosefet Ofek 2022 as increased from September 2023 for rank %the rank%
    MEANS
    CONSIDER `the table`
    WHEN `the BA table — rating code 101` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the rank` AT MOST 1 THEN 1_585.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 2  THEN 1_335.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 3  THEN 1_085.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 4  THEN 835.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 5  THEN 585.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 6  THEN 335.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 7  THEN 185.54
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 8  THEN 35.54
               OTHERWISE                    0
    WHEN `the MA table — rating code 102` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the rank` AT MOST 1 THEN 1_664.87
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 2  THEN 1_402.37
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 3  THEN 1_139.87
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 4  THEN 877.37
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 5  THEN 614.87
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 6  THEN 352.37
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 7  THEN 194.87
               IF `the rank` EQUALS 8  THEN 37.37
               OTHERWISE                    0

-- 2022 § 5.3: unlike a § 39 role supplement, Tosefet Ofek 2022 IS pro-rated
-- "in proportion to the fraction of the post, compared with a teacher on a
-- full post". The two payments therefore behave differently on a half post,
-- which is the sort of thing a payslip gets wrong.
GIVEN `the table` IS A `a salary table`
      `the rank` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of a full post` IS A NUMBER
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the table` `the rank` `the fraction of a full post` `the date`
    @nlg Tosefet Ofek 2022 payable at rank %the rank%
    MEANS
    IF `the date` `is before` `the date tosefet ofek 2022 takes effect`
        THEN 0
        ELSE `the amount at the date` TIMES `the fraction of a full post`
    WHERE
        `the amount at the date` MEANS
            IF `the date` `is before` `the date tosefet ofek 2022 is increased`
                THEN `tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2022 in` `the table` `the rank`
                ELSE `tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2023 in` `the table` `the rank`

§§ `Section 22 of the 2022 agreement — the school-role supplement`

-- The principal designates school roles and allots each between two and five
-- whole UNITS; a unit is 200 shekels a month (2022 § 22.4). It is unlike
-- everything above it in three ways, all of them expressly stated: it is not
-- part of the combined salary and does not enter the base of any other
-- supplement (§ 22.11); it is paid at its FULL shekel value to a part-time
-- teacher, provided the post is at least a third (§ 22.9); and no study-fund
-- contribution is made on it (§ 22.12).
`the value of one school-role unit` MEANS 200        -- 2022 § 22.4
`the fewest units a school role may carry` MEANS 2   -- 2022 § 22.2
`the most units a school role may carry` MEANS 5     -- 2022 § 22.2
`the smallest post that carries the school-role supplement` MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY 3  -- 2022 § 22.6, § 22.9

-- 2022 § 22.1 set this running from the school year beginning 1.9.2025. The
-- approved collective agreement of 29.6.2026, § 19, replaced that with the
-- school year beginning 1.9.2026 — one of the economies the wage-reduction
-- agreement paid for. Both dates are carried, because a computation about
-- the 2025/26 school year and one about 2026/27 need different answers.
`the date section 22 was first to take effect` MEANS YMD 2025 9 1
`the date section 22 takes effect as postponed` MEANS YMD 2026 9 1

GIVEN `the units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the units are within the section 22 range` IF
        `the units` AT LEAST `the fewest units a school role may carry`
    AND `the units` AT MOST `the most units a school role may carry`

GIVEN `the units` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of a full post` IS A NUMBER
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the school-role supplement for` `the units` `the fraction of a full post` `the date`
    @nlg the school-role supplement for %the units% units
    MEANS
    IF       `the date` `is before` `the date section 22 takes effect as postponed`
         OR  NOT (`the units are within the section 22 range` `the units`)
         OR  `the fraction of a full post` BELOW `the smallest post that carries the school-role supplement`
        THEN 0
        -- § 22.9 and § 22.10: the full shekel value, whether the post is a
        -- third or more than whole. There is no pro-rating in either
        -- direction.
        ELSE `the units` TIMES `the value of one school-role unit`

§§ `Illustrations`

`the first day of the 2024 school year` MEANS YMD 2024 9 1
`a day in the 2022 school year` MEANS YMD 2022 10 1
`a day in the 2026 school year` MEANS YMD 2026 10 1

-- § 39(a): the rates, read back against the article.
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` `a primary school` 0 EQUALS 10%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `homeroom teacher of a first-grade class` `a primary school` 0 EQUALS 11.5%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `subject coordinator` `a primary school` 0 EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `subject coordinator` `a junior high school` 0 EQUALS 8%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `social-education coordinator` `a junior high school` 0 EQUALS 10%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `laboratory coordinator` `a primary school` 0 EQUALS 3%

-- § 39(a)(9): the grade-coordinator rate FALLS as the grade grows.
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `grade-level coordinator` `a primary school` 4 EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT `the section 39 rate for` `grade-level coordinator` `a primary school` 5 EQUALS 6%

-- § 39(b): a third of a post carries the supplements; below that, nothing.
#ASSERT `the post carries the role supplements` (50%)
#ASSERT NOT `the post carries the role supplements` 0.3

-- § 39(c): two supplements, or three with the district director's approval.
#ASSERT `the number of role supplements is allowed` 2 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the number of role supplements is allowed` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `the number of role supplements is allowed` 3 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the number of role supplements is allowed` 4 TRUE

-- 2022 § 10.1: the floor bites at the bottom of the table and not at the top.
-- On a rank-1 BA salary of 6,300 the homeroom supplement would be 630, so the
-- 1,000 floor lifts it; on 12,000 the 10% is 1,200 and the floor is idle.
#ASSERT `the role supplement for` `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` `a junior high school` 0 6_300 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_000
#ASSERT `the role supplement for` `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` `a junior high school` 0 12_000 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_200

-- Before 1.9.2023 there was no floor, so the same rank-1 teacher had 630.
#ASSERT `the role supplement for` `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` `a junior high school` 0 6_300 `a day in the 2022 school year` EQUALS 630

-- A supplement outside 2022 § 10 has no floor at any date.
#ASSERT `the role supplement for` `laboratory coordinator` `a primary school` 0 6_300 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 189

-- 2022 § 5: Tosefet Ofek 2022 falls as the rank rises, and is nil at rank 9.
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 1 1 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_585.54
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 9 1 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the MA table — rating code 102` 1 1 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_664.87

-- It doubled on 1.9.2023, and was nil before it began.
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 1 1 `a day in the 2022 school year` EQUALS 792.77
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 1 1 (YMD 2022 1 1) EQUALS 0

-- 2022 § 5.3: it IS pro-rated, unlike a § 39 role supplement.
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 1 (50%) `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 792.77

-- THE CONTRAST WORTH SEEING. On the same half post, at the same moment, the
-- homeroom supplement is paid WHOLE and Tosefet Ofek 2022 is paid HALF. Both
-- are stated expressly — 2008 § 39(b) and 2022 § 5.3 — and they point in
-- opposite directions.
#ASSERT `the role supplement for` `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade` `a junior high school` 0 12_000 `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_200
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 for` `the BA table — rating code 101` 4 (50%) `the first day of the 2024 school year` EQUALS 417.77

-- 2022 § 22, as postponed by the 2026 agreement § 19: nothing is payable in
-- the 2025/26 school year, and three units are worth 600 a month from
-- 1.9.2026.
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 3 1 (YMD 2025 10 1) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 3 1 `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 5 1 `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 1_000

-- § 22.2: fewer than two units or more than five is not a school role.
#ASSERT NOT `the units are within the section 22 range` 1
#ASSERT `the units are within the section 22 range` 2
#ASSERT `the units are within the section 22 range` 5
#ASSERT NOT `the units are within the section 22 range` 6
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 1 1 `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 0

-- § 22.9 and § 22.10: the full shekel value on a third of a post, and on
-- more than a whole one; nothing below a third.
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 3 (1 DIVIDED BY 3) `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 3 1.2 `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the school-role supplement for` 3 0.3 `a day in the 2026 school year` EQUALS 0
